/E (The Freedom in Africa Report \(F[in]AR 2026\) provides a comparative assessment of conditions across African countries by examining three broad areas: Political Freedom, Economic Freedom, and Prosperity. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1007 0 R
/E (These dimensions when considered together provide a wider picture of how political rights, economic conditions, and living standards interact in shaping the experience of freedom across the continent.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1117 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1007 0 R
/E (F[in]AR 2026 is based entirely on secondary data. Rather than generating its own surveys or collecting information directly from countries, the report uses established international and African datasets, indexes, and statistical sources. The indicators were selected based on their relevance to the three F[in]AR dimensions, their availability across African countries, and the credibility and consistency of the organisations responsible for producing the data.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1007 0 R
/E (For this edition, the assessment primarily uses the most recent data reported for 2026. Where a 2026 figure was not yet available, the latest available data from 2025 was used instead. This approach allows the report to incorporate the newest information available while avoiding the use of estimates where reliable, published figures were not yet available.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
