1449 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1015 0 R
/E (Political Freedom in Africa at a Glance)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1450 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1015 0 R
/E (Political freedom refers to the extent to which people can participate freely in public and political life without undue interference or repression. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1451 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1015 0 R
/E (It encompasses the ability to vote and choose leaders, express opinions, access independent media, organise and protest peacefully, and receive fair treatment from political and judicial institutions. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1452 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1015 0 R
/E (The index recorded a clear improvement in the 2026 dataset, with the overall average rising from 47 in 2025 to 52.8 in 2026. The gains across electoral integrity, freedom of speech, press freedom, freedom of assembly, judicial independence, and protection from oppression and torture suggest that the political liberty measure expanded in a number of African countries. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1453 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1015 0 R
/E (However, the improvement should not be interpreted as a continent-wide reversal of democratic decline. The individual indicators reveal substantial setbacks in countries such as Chad, Burundi, Cameroon, Egypt and Equatorial Guinea, while judicial independence remained especially uneven.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1454 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1015 0 R
/E (The International Institute for Democracy and Electoral Assistance \(International IDEA\) similarly identifies fragile institutions, electoral manipulation and human-rights abuses as continuing pressures on democratic consolidation in Africa. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1455 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1015 0 R
/E (Public demand for political freedoms also remains strong. Afrobarometer found that 65% of citizens surveyed across 38 African countries feel at least somewhat free to express their views, although that figure has declined over the longer term. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1456 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1015 0 R
/E (The 2026 outlook is therefore cautiously positive: Africa's political freedom score has improved, but the uneven country-level results show that democratic gains remain fragile and far from secure.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
