1489 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1017 0 R
/E (It notes that cumbersome start-up requirements discourage formal business startups, while simpler processes can support job creation and more private-sector growth. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1490 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1017 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1491 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1017 0 R
/E (At the other end, Somalia fell to 0.1, while Burundi, Chad, the Central African Republic and Sudan all recorded very low scores.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1492 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1017 0 R
/E (The contrast in this dataset is therefore significant. A few African countries appear increasingly supportive of new businesses, while several fragile economies remain difficult environments for formal enterprise. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1493 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1017 0 R
/E (With many countries moving backwards, the 2026 figures show that Africa's progress in business creation is highly unequal, with administrative barriers continuing to limit entrepreneurship in parts of the continent.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
1494 0 obj
<<
