/E (The top 10 are Seychelles \(8.7\), Mauritius \(8.4\), Algeria \(7.4\), Egypt \(7.2\), Cape Verde \(7.0\), Ghana \(6.9\), Tunisia \(6.9\), Senegal \(6.8\), Morocco \(6.6\), and Botswana \(6.5\), while the bottom 10 are Eritrea \(4.7\), Eswatini \(4.7\), Guinea-Bissau \(4.7\), Angola \(4.7\), Chad \(3.8\), Niger \(3.8\), DR Congo \(3.7\), Central African Republic \(3.6\), Somalia \(2.9\), and South Sudan \(1.7\).)
