/E (This is what makes progress in Central Africa particularly challenging: problems in one area often appear alongside problems in another, leaving fewer areas of strength to offset them. Unlike regions where strong political institutions or stronger economies can lift a country's overall position, several Central African countries face weaknesses across multiple parts of the freedom and prosperity picture at the same time.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [13]
>>
